# Hot-path data (§14.5)

**Per-part, per-stud, per-instance and per-vehicle-car data never becomes a JS object.** It lives in typed arrays or GPU buffers and is addressed by integer handles.

| Data | Representation |
|---|---|
| Chunk placements | SoA per chunk: `Int32Array` x/z, `Int16Array` yPlates, `Uint8Array` rot, `Uint32Array` refId, `Uint8Array` flags, free-list |
| Bake instance lists | `Uint32Array` partId, `Uint16Array` colorId, `Float32Array` 12-float matrices |
| Stud visibility | `Uint32Array` bitsets per model and per chunk |
| Occupancy | `Uint8Array` or `Uint16Array` column grids per chunk |
| Render instances | GPU buffers from pooled pages; CPU mirrors are typed arrays only |
| Sim state | `Float64Array` offsets and speeds, `Int32Array` edge ids, index ranges per consist |
| Track graph | CSR in `Int32Array`s |
| Element existence | sorted `Uint32Array` of packed (part, color) keys plus binary search |

**On frame, tick and per-element loops:**
- No allocations at all: no closures, `.map`, `.filter`, `for…of` iterators, spreads, destructuring of fresh objects, template strings, or `Map`/`Set` keyed per part.
- Use indexed `for` loops, preallocated scratch arrays at module or class scope, and out-parameters (`out: Float64Array`).
- `bigint` exact poses belong only to editing, joining and validation. Sim and render read float64/float32 data derived from exact poses.
- Render and validation work relative to the chunk origin (`floor(x/640)`). Never put large world coordinates into float32.
- Cross-thread bulk data travels as **transferable** typed arrays through `rpc`. Don't send arrays of objects.

**Cold data may use objects:** catalog metadata, profiles, plan footprints, UI view models, and a selection facade. The domain exposes **views** (`ChunkView`, `PlacementHandle`) over the arrays, not object copies.

Every new hot loop needs a `*.bench.ts` with an allocation probe.
